  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Added a reproducible process-isolated macOS arm64 witness and recorded full verified M1 Max results against SageMath 10.9.post2. Native FLINT, M4RI, and FFLAS-FFPACK production kernels build and run as Mach-O arm64; the checked JSON now persists exact pnpm, clang, FLINT, file-identity, linkage, and Accelerate evidence. Unlike serialization formats have null ratios and single-runtime Markdown is explicitly labeled. The witness isolates general word-prime public representation and exact polynomial construction as the main boundary regressions.",
    "risks": [
      "General word-prime matrix construction is 15.38x and formatting is 13.43x slower than SageMath; the runtime-local 300 by 300 SagePack witness takes 1.37 seconds to dump and 0.47 seconds to load, without comparison to SageMath's different serialization format. Row and column swaps are not implemented and successful backend routes are not traced.",
      "The first pnpm native:precompile:production run on macOS linked its addon but hit a transient node-gyp ENOENT for build/node_gyp_bins; a cached rerun completed all twelve kernels.",
      "Sage.js SagePack and SageMath Python serialization are different formats, so serialization bytes and absolute timings are intentionally not treated as cross-runtime equivalence claims.",
      "Early Linux validation attempts in the receipt history failed before this worktree was built and its shared native cache restored; the later full native suite and all focused checks pass."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Give general word-prime matrices a bulk public construction/format/serialization path, add swaps, and emit SAGEJS_NATIVE_TRACE routes without weakening FFLAS-FFPACK performance.",
      "Profile bulk ZZ[x] and QQ[x] resource construction on both Linux x64 and macOS arm64.",
      "Add a clean macOS CI/build witness for the transient node-gyp post-link node_gyp_bins failure and make first-run publication deterministic.",
      "Retain benchmark history across CPU families and compare later revisions with the checked raw JSON rather than hard-coding one host's crossover."
    ]
  }
}
